---@class cloudflare.firewall.CreateLockdownRequest
---@field zone_id string Defines an identifier.
---@field configurations cloudflare.firewall.LockdownConfigurationsList A list of IP addresses or CIDR ranges that will be allowed to access the URLs specified in the Zone Lockdown rule. You can include any number of `ip` or `ip_range` configurations.
---@field urls cloudflare.firewall.LockdownsCreateRequestUrlsList The URLs to include in the current WAF override. You can use wildcards. Each entered URL will be escaped before use, which means you can only use simple wildcard patterns.
---@field description? string An informative summary of the rule. This value is sanitized and any tags will be removed.
---@field paused? boolean When true, indicates that the rule is currently paused.
---@field priority? number The priority of the rule to control the processing order. A lower number indicates higher priority. If not provided, any rules with a configured priority will be processed before rules without a priority.

